    "question": {
      ":question/id": "603f35af-30d8-543d-b314-b7c517e79ec7",
      ":question/problem": "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$ and points the same direction.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{a}}{|\\mathbf{a}|}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\mathbf{a}| &= \\sqrt{(-7)^2+(8)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{113} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{113}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor a radical denominator, use $\\sqrt{R}\\,\\sqrt{R}=R$ to simplify the components; equivalently, $1/\\sqrt{R}=\\sqrt{R}/R$ for $R>0$.\n\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{a}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{u} &= \\frac{\\mathbf{a}}{|\\mathbf{a}|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{113}}\\cdot (\\mathbf{a}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{113}}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{7 \\sqrt{113}}{113} \\\\ \\frac{8 \\sqrt{113}}{113}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/requires-calculator": false,
